From: Ci4Rail <engineering@ci4rail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: retry recovery SD CMD8 after a short delay

Some recovery SD cards time out on their first CMD8 but respond after
50 ms. Retry once on timeout for MMC1 in U-Boot proper. Preserve the
same retry on the existing UHS fallback attempt, without diagnostic
prints. Leave SPL, eMMC and the normal protocol fallback unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ModuCop recovery SD workaround]

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/mmc.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/mmc.c
@@ -2905,6 +2905,12 @@
 
 	/* Test for SD version 2 */
 	err = mmc_send_if_cond(mmc);
+	/* Allow a slow-starting recovery SD card one delayed CMD8 retry. */
+	if (err == -ETIMEDOUT && !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SPL_BUILD) &&
+	    mmc_get_blk_desc(mmc)->devnum == 1) {
+		mdelay(50);
+		err = mmc_send_if_cond(mmc);
+	}
 
 	/* Now try to get the SD card's operating condition */
 	err = sd_send_op_cond(mmc, uhs_en);
